-- title:
--   Original variable-endpoint C1 positive-error absorption under exhausting BV source localisation
-- statement:
--   For the genuine original bounded-variation spectrally negative Levy process X and admissible dividend strategy D, every sample-dependent stopped physical grid with last endpoint bounded by T has its actual discounted C1 Taylor source error positive expectation converging to zero. Interior localisation bands can vary with the exhausting event index. On each fixed event the original fine-cell and source-variation hypotheses give L1 convergence; outside the event a uniform original BV source-mass bound controls the positive error. Full positive-error integrability is derived from a single event's masked integrability, a.e. strong measurability, and original BV source-mass integrability, rather than assumed. No signed or prebudget theorem is imported. The off-event source domination and appropriate contact/cap control remain explicit source-instantiation obligations.
-- source:
--   Source-specific composition of avram_bv_error7 original event variable-prefix positive-error L1 and original source-mass event-tail absorption. Conditional adapter toward stopped-grid Fatou.

